00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Week one, we talked about how our screens are one of the primary instruments of formation as humans. The screens consume our time and therefore are making us into a certain type of person.

27
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:54,000
We realize it or not. They become so intertwined into our everyday lives that we don't even realize how much they're forming us, or how often they're forming us.

28
00:06:54,000 --> 00:07:03,000
And Michelle talked about Romans 12:1 and 2, that we are to be transformed by the renewing of our mind, not to be conformed into the image of this world, but transformed.

29
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:12,000
And the screens play a really important role in that. And then week two, we said our screens are often pumping our minds and our hearts with voices of people and

30
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:23,000
things that are competing with Jesus for the allegiance of our lives. We are getting voices and encouragement to follow after things that are less than the thing we were made to follow after.

31
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:32,000
And that is the voice of the Good Shepherd, who leads us to abundant life. And then last week, we talked about that. Of all of those voices, there's one primary influencing voice behind all of them.

32
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:41,000
And that's the voice of the serpent in the garden, who comes to Adam and Eve and who comes to each one of us through our screens and our devices and promises us a

